(function(E){ const x = E["exam-07"] = E["exam-07"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x07-l3"] = {"id":"x07-l3","patterns":["L3-humanities","PARA-opinion"],"title":{"en":"Listening Part 3: planning a report","tr":"Listening Part 3: bir rapor planlamak","fa":"Listening Part 3: برنامه‌ریزی یک گزارش"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to answer A-C questions on two students’ reasons, problems and opinions, and to match four places to what made each one different, using a box of six.","tr":"Bu derste iki öğrencinin nedenleri, sorunları ve görüşleri hakkındaki A-C sorularını cevaplamayı ve dört yeri, her birini farklı kılan şeyle altılı bir kutudan eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری به سؤال‌های A-C درباره‌ی دلیل‌ها، مشکل‌ها و نظرهای دو دانشجو جواب بدهی و چهار جا را با چیزی که هر کدام را متفاوت کرده، از یک کادر شش‌تایی، جور کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Listening Part 3: planning a report","tr":"Listening Part 3: bir rapor planlamak","fa":"Listening Part 3: برنامه‌ریزی یک گزارش"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to answer A-C questions on two students’ reasons, problems and opinions, and to match four places to what made each one different, using a box of six.","tr":"Bu derste iki öğrencinin nedenleri, sorunları ve görüşleri hakkındaki A-C sorularını cevaplamayı ve dört yeri, her birini farklı kılan şeyle altılı bir kutudan eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری به سؤال‌های A-C درباره‌ی دلیل‌ها، مشکل‌ها و نظرهای دو دانشجو جواب بدهی و چهار جا را با چیزی که هر کدام را متفاوت کرده، از یک کادر شش‌تایی، جور کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"10"},{"label":{"en":"Speakers","tr":"Konuşan","fa":"گوینده"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Options in the box","tr":"Kutudaki seçenek","fa":"گزینه‌های کادر"},"value":"A-F"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: museum audio guides","tr":"Bu sınav: müze sesli rehberleri","fa":"این آزمون: راهنماهای صوتی موزه"},"intro":{"en":"Part 3 is always about study. Projects in the arts, media and culture are a large part of the humanities topics, which together are the most common Part 3 subject.","tr":"Part 3 her zaman ders çalışmayla ilgilidir. Sanat, medya ve kültür projeleri beşerî konuların büyük bir kısmını oluşturur; bu konular birlikte Part 3’ün en sık konusudur.","fa":"Part 3 همیشه درباره‌ی درس است. پروژه‌های هنر، رسانه و فرهنگ بخش بزرگی از موضوع‌های علوم انسانی‌اند که روی‌هم رایج‌ترین موضوع Part 3 هستند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x07-l3-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["L3-humanities","PARA-opinion"],"often":{"pattern":"L3-humanities","n":21,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 21 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 21’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۱ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Two students plan a research report","tr":"İki öğrenci bir araştırma raporu planlıyor","fa":"دو دانشجو گزارش یک پژوهش را برنامه‌ریزی می‌کنند"},"asks":{"en":"Two students plan the sections of a report on something visitors use at museums: why they chose it, its history, a problem with their survey, their views and recommendation, and then a comparison of four places they visited.","tr":"İki öğrenci, ziyaretçilerin müzelerde kullandığı bir şey hakkındaki raporun bölümlerini planlıyor: neden seçtikleri, tarihçesi, anketlerindeki bir sorun, görüşleri ve önerileri, sonra ziyaret ettikleri dört yerin karşılaştırması.","fa":"دو دانشجو بخش‌های گزارشی را درباره‌ی وسیله‌ای که بازدیدکننده‌ها در موزه‌ها استفاده می‌کنند برنامه‌ریزی می‌کنند: چرا انتخابش کردند، تاریخچه‌اش، مشکلی در نظرسنجی‌شان، نظرها و پیشنهادشان و بعد مقایسه‌ی چهار جایی که رفته‌اند."},"fields":["Why this topic","History","A problem with the survey","Views on apps","The main advantage","Recommendation","Four places compared"],"words":[{"a":"it started when","b":"what got me interested was","tr":"... ile başladı","fa":"از وقتی شروع شد که"},{"a":"I’d assumed","b":"I thought, wrongly, that","tr":"... sanmıştım","fa":"خیال می‌کردم"},{"a":"limitation","b":"a weakness in the research","tr":"sınırlılık","fa":"محدودیت"},{"a":"I’m not convinced","b":"I doubt it / I’m not sure","tr":"ikna olmadım","fa":"قانع نشده‌ام"},{"a":"I see what you mean","b":"I partly agree","tr":"ne demek istediğini anlıyorum","fa":"منظورت را می‌فهمم"},{"a":"the main advantage","b":"the real benefit / the best thing","tr":"asıl avantaj","fa":"مزیت اصلی"},{"a":"freedom","b":"you can go wherever you like","tr":"özgürlük","fa":"آزادی"},{"a":"recommend","b":"suggest one main change","tr":"önermek","fa":"پیشنهاد کردن"},{"a":"aimed at","b":"designed for","tr":"... yönelik","fa":"مخصوصِ، برای"},{"a":"stood out","b":"was what made it different","tr":"öne çıktı","fa":"برجسته بود"},{"a":"hidden","b":"hard to see / not noticed","tr":"gizli","fa":"پنهان"},{"a":"overseas tourists","b":"visitors from other countries","tr":"yabancı turistler","fa":"گردشگرهای خارجی"}],"traps":[{"en":"A reason ruled out twice: \"It wasn’t her idea... and it isn’t true that... For me it really started when...\" Choose the last reason.","tr":"İki kez elenen bir neden: \"Onun fikri değildi... ve ... doğru değil... Benim için asıl ... ile başladı.\" Son nedeni seç.","fa":"دلیلی که دو بار رد می‌شود: «ایده‌ی او نبود... و درست نیست که... برای من در واقع از وقتی شروع شد که...». دلیل آخر را انتخاب کن."},{"en":"In the matching task, a place may have two features from the box. Choose the one the speakers say made it different.","tr":"Eşleştirmede bir yerin kutudan iki özelliği olabilir. Konuşanların onu farklı kılan şey dediğini seç.","fa":"در تمرین جورکردن، ممکن است یک جا دو ویژگی از کادر داشته باشد. چیزی را انتخاب کن که گوینده‌ها می‌گویند آن را متفاوت کرده."},{"en":"A wrong guess corrected by the other speaker: \"You could download it, couldn’t you?\" \"No, none of them...\"","tr":"Diğer konuşanın düzelttiği yanlış bir tahmin: \"İndirebiliyordun, değil mi?\" \"Hayır, hiçbiri...\"","fa":"حدس غلطی که گوینده‌ی دیگر اصلاحش می‌کند: «می‌شد دانلودش کرد، نه؟» «نه، هیچ‌کدام...»."}],"example":{"lines":[["Student A","The castle’s café was very expensive."],["Student B","It was, but lots of places are. What made it special was the view from the tower."]],"item":"The castle: A It was expensive.  B It had a special view.","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Expensive is true but \"lots of places are\". \"What made it special\" gives the answer.","tr":"Pahalı olması doğru ama \"birçok yer öyle\". \"Onu özel yapan şey\" cevabı veriyor.","fa":"گران بودن درست است، اما «خیلی جاها این‌طورند». «چیزی که خاصش کرد» جواب را می‌دهد."}}},{"id":"L3-arts","ctx":["L3-arts","L3-humanities"],"title":{"en":"Arts, literature and media","tr":"Sanat, edebiyat ve medya","fa":"هنر، ادبیات و رسانه"},"asks":{"en":"Two students, sometimes with a tutor, plan or review a project on a play, a book, a film, newspapers or an art form. Questions ask what they decide, what they think of a source or a method, what went wrong and what they will do next.","tr":"İki öğrenci, bazen bir hocayla, bir oyun, bir kitap, bir film, gazeteler ya da bir sanat dalı üzerine bir projeyi planlar ya da değerlendirir. Sorular neye karar verdiklerini, bir kaynak ya da yöntem hakkında ne düşündüklerini, neyin ters gittiğini ve sırada ne yapacaklarını sorar.","fa":"دو دانشجو، گاهی با یک استاد، پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی یک نمایش، یک کتاب، یک فیلم، روزنامه‌ها یا یک هنر را برنامه‌ریزی یا بررسی می‌کنند. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند به چه تصمیمی می‌رسند، درباره‌ی یک منبع یا روش چه فکر می‌کنند، چه چیزی خراب شد و قدم بعدی‌شان چیست."},"fields":["What did the students find surprising about the play?","What do they decide to include in the presentation?","What is their opinion of each source?","Which TWO problems did they have with the archive?","What will they do next?"],"words":[{"a":"adaptation","b":"the film version of the novel","tr":"uyarlama","fa":"اقتباس"},{"a":"audience","b":"the people watching","tr":"seyirci","fa":"تماشاگران"},{"a":"critic","b":"the reviewer / the person who wrote about it","tr":"eleştirmen","fa":"منتقد"},{"a":"archive","b":"the old records the library keeps","tr":"arşiv","fa":"آرشیو"},{"a":"primary source","b":"a document from the time itself","tr":"birincil kaynak","fa":"منبع دست‌اول"},{"a":"illustration","b":"the pictures in the book","tr":"resim, illüstrasyon","fa":"تصویرگری"},{"a":"character","b":"a person in the story","tr":"karakter","fa":"شخصیت"},{"a":"setting","b":"where and when the story happens","tr":"olayın geçtiği yer ve zaman","fa":"زمان و مکان داستان"},{"a":"outdated","b":"it feels old-fashioned now","tr":"modası geçmiş","fa":"قدیمی‌شده"},{"a":"appeal to","b":"children love it / it attracts","tr":"... -e hitap etmek","fa":"جذاب بودن برای"},{"a":"coverage","b":"how the papers reported it","tr":"haber yapılış biçimi","fa":"پوشش خبری"},{"a":"exaggerated","b":"made it sound bigger than it was","tr":"abartılı","fa":"اغراق‌آمیز"},{"a":"handout","b":"the sheet we give the class","tr":"dağıtılan not","fa":"جزوه"}],"traps":[{"en":"Views on a source change: \"it looked useful at first, but it’s too general\". The final view is the answer.","tr":"Kaynak hakkındaki görüş değişir: \"ilk başta işe yarar görünüyordu ama çok genel\". Cevap son görüştür.","fa":"نظر درباره‌ی یک منبع عوض می‌شود: «اولش مفید به نظر می‌رسید، ولی خیلی کلی است». جواب نظر آخر است."},{"en":"Original and version: the students compare the book and the film. Check which one the question is about.","tr":"Asıl eser ve uyarlama: öğrenciler kitabı ve filmi karşılaştırır. Sorunun hangisiyle ilgili olduğuna bak.","fa":"اصل و اقتباس: دانشجوها کتاب و فیلم را مقایسه می‌کنند. ببین سؤال درباره‌ی کدام است."}],"example":{"lines":[["Amy","The old film is closer to the novel than the new one."],["Tom","Closer in the story, maybe, but the new one feels much more like the book to me."],["Amy","Hmm, fair point. The atmosphere is better in the new one."]],"item":"What do the students agree about the new film?  A It follows the story more closely.   B It has a better atmosphere.   C It is too long.","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Amy first prefers the old film, then says \"fair point\": they agree the new one has a better atmosphere.","tr":"Amy önce eski filmi tercih ediyor, sonra \"fair point\" diyor: yeni filmin atmosferinin daha iyi olduğunda anlaşıyorlar.","fa":"امی اول فیلم قدیمی را ترجیح می‌دهد، بعد می‌گوید «fair point»: توافق می‌کنند که فضای فیلم جدید بهتر است."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L3-humanities"],"often":{"pattern":"L3-humanities","n":21,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 21 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 21’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۱ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Six A-C questions, then a box of six","tr":"Altı A-C sorusu, sonra altılı bir kutu","fa":"شش سؤال A-C، بعد یک کادر شش‌تایی"},"body":{"en":"Questions 21-26: choose A, B or C. Questions 27-30: four places and a box of six features, A-F; choose FOUR answers, each letter once. You read Questions 21-26 first and Questions 27-30 in the break.","tr":"Soru 21-26: A, B ya da C’yi seç. Soru 27-30: dört yer ve A-F arası altı özellikli bir kutu; DÖRT cevap seç, her harf bir kez. Önce Soru 21-26’yı, molada Soru 27-30’u okursun.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۱ تا ۲۶: A، B یا C را انتخاب کن. سؤال‌های ۲۷ تا ۳۰: چهار جا و کادری با شش ویژگی، A تا F؛ چهار جواب انتخاب کن، هر حرف یک بار. اول ۲۱ تا ۲۶ را می‌خوانی و در وقفه ۲۷ تا ۳۰ را."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Wait for the final view","tr":"Son görüşü bekle","fa":"منتظر نظر نهایی بمان"},"steps":[{"en":"Read each question and its three options; underline what makes them different.","tr":"Her soruyu ve üç seçeneğini oku; onları farklı kılan şeyin altını çiz.","fa":"هر سؤال و سه گزینه‌اش را بخوان؛ زیر چیزی که آن‌ها را متفاوت می‌کند خط بکش."},{"en":"Expect both speakers to mention wrong options; the answer often comes after not, but or actually.","tr":"İki konuşanın da yanlış seçeneklerden söz etmesini bekle; cevap çoğu zaman not, but ya da actually’den sonra gelir.","fa":"انتظار داشته باش هر دو گوینده از گزینه‌های غلط حرف بزنند؛ جواب اغلب بعد از not، but یا actually می‌آید."},{"en":"For the box, listen for each place’s name, then for \"what made it different\" or \"what stood out\".","tr":"Kutu için her yerin adını, sonra \"what made it different\" ya da \"what stood out\" ifadesini dinle.","fa":"برای کادر، به اسم هر جا گوش بده و بعد به «what made it different» یا «what stood out»."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"True, but not the answer","tr":"Doğru ama cevap değil","fa":"درست، اما جواب نیست"},"body":{"en":"In the matching task, a speaker may say something true about a place that is also true of other places: \"Their shop is huge, though... but lots of places have big shops.\" The answer is the feature that belongs to this place.","tr":"Eşleştirmede konuşan, bir yer hakkında diğer yerler için de doğru olan bir şey söyleyebilir: \"Dükkânları çok büyük ama... birçok yerin büyük dükkânı var.\" Cevap, bu yere ait olan özelliktir.","fa":"در تمرین جورکردن ممکن است گوینده چیزی درست درباره‌ی یک جا بگوید که درباره‌ی جاهای دیگر هم درست است: «فروشگاهشان خیلی بزرگ است... اما خیلی جاها فروشگاه بزرگ دارند». جواب ویژگی‌ای است که مال همین جاست."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"An opinion question, step by step","tr":"Bir görüş sorusu, adım adım","fa":"یک سؤال نظر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.","item":"What does the man think of online tickets? A They are cheaper.  B They are more convenient.  C They cause problems for some visitors.","lines":[["Man","The price is the same, so that’s not it. Yes, it’s quicker for most people, but I worry about visitors without smartphones. They get turned away at the door."]],"answer":"C","walk":[{"en":"A: \"The price is the same\" = no.","tr":"A: \"Fiyat aynı\" = hayır.","fa":"A: «قیمت یکی است» یعنی نه."},{"en":"B: he accepts it is quicker, but \"but I worry\" shows this is not his main view.","tr":"B: daha hızlı olduğunu kabul ediyor ama \"ama endişeliyim\" bunun ana görüşü olmadığını gösteriyor.","fa":"B: قبول دارد سریع‌تر است، اما «اما نگرانم» نشان می‌دهد این نظر اصلی‌اش نیست."},{"en":"C: visitors without smartphones \"get turned away\" = problems for some visitors.","tr":"C: akıllı telefonu olmayan ziyaretçiler \"kapıdan çevriliyor\" = bazı ziyaretçiler için sorun.","fa":"C: بازدیدکننده‌هایی که گوشی هوشمند ندارند «دمِ در برگردانده می‌شوند» یعنی برای بعضی‌ها مشکل‌ساز است."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"\"The gallery’s café was lovely, but plenty of galleries have nice cafés. What was unusual was that the guides were all artists.\" What made the gallery different?","options":["Its guides were artists.","It had a lovely café.","It was free."],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The café is true but common (\"plenty of galleries\"). \"What was unusual\" gives the answer.","tr":"Kafe doğru ama yaygın (\"pek çok galeride var\"). \"Alışılmadık olan\" cevabı veriyor.","fa":"کافه درست است، اما رایج («خیلی از گالری‌ها دارند»). «چیزی که غیرعادی بود» جواب را می‌دهد."}},"remember":{"en":"Let each option be mentioned, wait for not, but or actually, and choose what made each place different.","tr":"Her seçenekten söz edilmesine izin ver, not, but ya da actually’yi bekle ve her yeri farklı kılan şeyi seç.","fa":"بگذار از همه‌ی گزینه‌ها حرف زده شود، منتظر not، but یا actually بمان و چیزی را انتخاب کن که هر جا را متفاوت کرده."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x07-l3-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-l3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"listening","part":"Listening Part 3","title":{"en":"A report on museum audio guides","tr":"Müze sesli rehberleri üzerine bir rapor","fa":"گزارشی درباره‌ی راهنماهای صوتی موزه"},"timed":7,"ctx":["L3-humanities"],"script":[{"who":"Tariq","line":"So, Leah, we need to agree on the structure of our report on museum audio guides. Can we start with why we chose the topic? The tutor asked us to explain that in the introduction."},{"who":"Leah","line":"Well, it wasn't her idea, was it? She suggested we look at museum shops. And it isn't true that nobody has written about audio guides; we found loads of articles. For me it really started when I was volunteering at the art gallery last summer. I noticed that hardly anyone picked up an audio guide, even though they were free."},{"who":"Tariq","line":"Right, that should go in. Then the history section. I was surprised by how old the idea is."},{"who":"Leah","line":"Me too. I'd assumed they came out of the technology boom, invented by some electronics company. But the earliest ones, back in the nineteen-fifties, were enormous: visitors carried a heavy radio set around their neck."},{"who":"Tariq","line":"It's a nice detail. I'll find a photo for that section. Now, the survey. We should be honest about what went wrong."},{"who":"Leah","line":"Definitely. People were very willing to answer, and the questions were short enough. The real problem was that the manager only let us stand by the exit. So we only spoke to people who were leaving, and we missed everyone who gave up halfway round."},{"who":"Tariq","line":"That's a fair point. We'll mention it as a limitation. It probably means our results make the guides look more popular than they really are, because the people who were enjoying the visit were the ones who stayed to the end. What about apps? A lot of museums are replacing their audio guides with apps you download onto your own phone."},{"who":"Leah","line":"It makes sense financially. What do you think?"},{"who":"Tariq","line":"I'm not convinced they're the answer. Lots of older visitors don't want to download anything, and your battery runs out by lunchtime. The museums save money, but I'm not sure visitors gain much."},{"who":"Leah","line":"Hmm. I think you're being a bit negative, but I see what you mean. So what would you say is the main advantage of a traditional guide?"},{"who":"Tariq","line":"Not the price, because a human guide on a group tour is often just as cheap per person. And the information isn't any more accurate. I think it's freedom: you can wander wherever you like and listen only to what interests you."},{"who":"Leah","line":"I agree. That came up again and again in our interviews. And our recommendation? We said we'd suggest one main change."},{"who":"Tariq","line":"We talked about offering more languages, and making them free everywhere. But most of the complaints were about length. So I'd recommend shorter recordings, no more than a minute for each object."},{"who":"Leah","line":"Agreed. People stop listening after about forty seconds anyway. Now, the comparison section. Shall we go through the four museums we visited?"},{"who":"Tariq","line":"Yes. The Riverside Museum first. Their guide was the one people used least. Most visitors didn't even notice the desk where you collect it, because it was hidden behind the shop. The recordings themselves were perfectly good, which made it even more of a shame."},{"who":"Leah","line":"True. Then the Gallery of Modern Art. I loved their guide, partly because each artwork is described by a different actor. It felt like listening to a radio play."},{"who":"Tariq","line":"It was very well made. Their recordings are long, though, some over three minutes."},{"who":"Leah","line":"They are. But the thing that made the Gallery's guide different was the actors. Lots of places have long recordings."},{"who":"Tariq","line":"OK. Then the Railway Museum. Their guide is aimed entirely at children, with games and a cartoon train driver."},{"who":"Leah","line":"Which is clever, because families are their main visitors. And the castle?"},{"who":"Tariq","line":"The castle's guide is available in fourteen languages, which is far more than anywhere else we went. They get a lot of overseas tourists."},{"who":"Leah","line":"You could also download it at home before the visit, couldn't you?"},{"who":"Tariq","line":"No, none of the four offered that, which surprised me. Anyway, the languages are what stood out at the castle."},{"who":"Leah","line":"Fine. Let's write up those four sections tonight and swap them tomorrow."}],"groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 21-26. Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":21,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Why did the students choose audio guides as their topic?","options":["A Their tutor suggested it.","B Very little had been written about it.","C Leah noticed something while volunteering."],"correct":2,"evidence":"when I was volunteering at the art gallery last summer","why":{"en":"The tutor suggested museum shops, and they \"found loads of articles\". It started when Leah was volunteering and saw that hardly anyone used the guides.","tr":"Hoca müze dükkânlarını önerdi ve \"bir sürü makale buldular\". Leah gönüllüyken neredeyse kimsenin rehberleri kullanmadığını görünce başladı.","fa":"استاد فروشگاه موزه را پیشنهاد داد و «کلی مقاله پیدا کردند». از وقتی شروع شد که لیا داوطلب بود و دید تقریباً کسی از راهنماها استفاده نمی‌کند."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":22,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What surprised Leah about the history of audio guides?","options":["A They were invented by an electronics company.","B The first ones were very large and heavy.","C They were first used in theatres."],"correct":1,"evidence":"visitors carried a heavy radio set around their neck","why":{"en":"She had \"assumed\" an electronics company invented them, but the earliest guides were \"enormous: a heavy radio set\".","tr":"Bir elektronik şirketinin icat ettiğini \"sanmıştı\", ama ilk rehberler \"kocamandı: ağır bir radyo\".","fa":"«خیال می‌کرد» یک شرکت الکترونیک اختراعش کرده، اما اولین راهنماها «غول‌پیکر بودند: یک دستگاه رادیوی سنگین»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":23,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What was the main problem with the students’ survey?","options":["A They could only ask people at the exit.","B Few visitors were willing to answer.","C The questions were too long."],"correct":0,"evidence":"the manager only let us stand by the exit","why":{"en":"People were \"very willing\" and the questions were \"short enough\". \"The manager only let us stand by the exit.\"","tr":"İnsanlar \"çok istekliydi\" ve sorular \"yeterince kısaydı\". \"Müdür yalnızca çıkışta durmamıza izin verdi.\"","fa":"آدم‌ها «خیلی مایل بودند» و سؤال‌ها «به اندازه‌ی کافی کوتاه بودند». «مدیر فقط اجازه داد کنار در خروج بایستیم»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":24,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What does Tariq think about museum apps?","options":["A They are the best way forward.","B They are too expensive for museums.","C They help museums more than visitors."],"correct":2,"evidence":"The museums save money, but I'm not sure visitors gain much","why":{"en":"He is \"not convinced\": \"The museums save money, but I’m not sure visitors gain much.\"","tr":"\"İkna olmadı\": \"Müzeler para tasarruf ediyor ama ziyaretçilerin pek bir şey kazandığından emin değilim.\"","fa":"«قانع نشده»: «موزه‌ها صرفه‌جویی می‌کنند، اما مطمئن نیستم بازدیدکننده‌ها چیز زیادی به دست بیاورند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":25,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What do the students agree is the main advantage of a traditional audio guide?","options":["A It is cheaper than a human guide.","B Visitors can choose what to listen to.","C Its information is more accurate."],"correct":1,"evidence":"you can wander wherever you like and listen only to what interests you","why":{"en":"\"Not the price\" and \"the information isn’t any more accurate\". The advantage is freedom: \"listen only to what interests you\".","tr":"\"Fiyat değil\" ve \"bilgi daha doğru değil\". Avantaj özgürlük: \"yalnızca ilgini çekeni dinle\".","fa":"«قیمت نیست» و «اطلاعاتش دقیق‌تر نیست». مزیتش آزادی است: «فقط به چیزی گوش بدهی که برایت جالب است»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":26,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What change will the students recommend?","options":["A shorter recordings","B more languages","C free guides in every museum"],"correct":0,"evidence":"I'd recommend shorter recordings, no more than a minute for each object","why":{"en":"More languages and free guides were only \"talked about\". \"Most of the complaints were about length\", so they recommend shorter recordings.","tr":"Daha çok dil ve ücretsiz rehberler yalnızca \"konuşuldu\". \"Şikâyetlerin çoğu uzunlukla ilgiliydi\", bu yüzden daha kısa kayıtlar öneriyorlar.","fa":"زبان‌های بیشتر و راهنمای رایگان فقط «مطرح شدند». «بیشترِ شکایت‌ها درباره‌ی طول بود»، پس ضبط‌های کوتاه‌تر را پیشنهاد می‌کنند."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 27-30. What do the students say about the audio guide at each of the following places? Choose FOUR answers from the box and write the correct letter, A-F, next to Questions 27-30.","qtype":"matching","bank":["A Its recordings are too long.","B Its descriptions are read by actors.","C It is available in many languages.","D It is designed for children.","E It can be downloaded at home.","F Few visitors use it."],"questions":[{"n":27,"kind":"match","prompt":"the Riverside Museum","correct":5,"evidence":"Their guide was the one people used least","why":{"en":"\"The one people used least\", because the desk was hidden behind the shop: F.","tr":"\"İnsanların en az kullandığı\", çünkü masa dükkânın arkasına gizlenmişti: F.","fa":"«کم‌استفاده‌ترین»، چون میز پشت فروشگاه پنهان بود: F."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":28,"kind":"match","prompt":"the Gallery of Modern Art","correct":1,"evidence":"each artwork is described by a different actor","why":{"en":"Long recordings are common (\"lots of places\"); what made it different was the actors: B.","tr":"Uzun kayıtlar yaygın (\"birçok yerde var\"); onu farklı kılan oyuncular: B.","fa":"ضبط طولانی رایج است («خیلی جاها»)؛ چیزی که آن را متفاوت کرد بازیگرها بودند: B."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":29,"kind":"match","prompt":"the Railway Museum","correct":3,"evidence":"Their guide is aimed entirely at children","why":{"en":"\"Aimed entirely at children, with games and a cartoon train driver\": D.","tr":"\"Tamamen çocuklara yönelik, oyunlar ve çizgi film makinistiyle\": D.","fa":"«کاملاً مخصوص بچه‌ها، با بازی و یک راننده‌ی کارتونیِ قطار»: D."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"match","prompt":"the castle","correct":2,"evidence":"The castle's guide is available in fourteen languages","why":{"en":"\"Available in fourteen languages\". Downloading at home is ruled out: \"none of the four offered that\": C.","tr":"\"On dört dilde mevcut\". Evde indirmek eleniyor: \"dördünden hiçbiri bunu sunmuyordu\": C.","fa":"«به چهارده زبان موجود است». دانلود در خانه رد می‌شود: «هیچ‌کدام از چهارتا این را نداشتند»: C."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]}]}],"audio":{"voices":{"Announcer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_george"},"role":"Recorded rubric"},"Leah":{"accent":"British (Southern English)","gender":"F","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bf_emma"},"role":"Student"},"Tariq":{"accent":"Australian","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_lewis","fallback":true,"note":"Australian wanted; no free Australian voice yet"},"role":"Student"}},"sequence":[{"type":"announcer","text":"Part 3. You will hear two students, Leah and Tariq, discussing their research report on museum audio guides. First, you have some time to look at Questions 21 to 26."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 21-26"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen carefully and answer Questions 21 to 26."},{"type":"sfx","note":"quiet library study room"},{"type":"lines","from":0,"to":13},{"type":"announcer","text":"Before you hear the rest of the discussion, you have some time to look at Questions 27 to 30."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 27-30"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen and answer Questions 27 to 30."},{"type":"lines","from":14,"to":23},{"type":"announcer","text":"That is the end of Part 3. You now have half a minute to check your answers.","after":30}]},"id":"c-x07-l3-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-l3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"In a recording, \"what really stood out was...\" introduces...","options":["a feature that was missing","something the speaker disliked","the feature that made something different"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"Stood out\" = was noticeable and different from the rest.","tr":"\"Stood out\" = dikkat çekiciydi, diğerlerinden farklıydı.","fa":"«stood out» یعنی به چشم آمد و با بقیه فرق داشت."}},{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"We’ll mention it as a limitation of the study.\" A limitation is...","options":["a main finding","a weakness that affects the results","a recommendation"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A limitation is something that makes the results less complete or reliable.","tr":"Sınırlılık, sonuçları daha az eksiksiz ya da güvenilir yapan şeydir.","fa":"محدودیت چیزی است که نتیجه‌ها را ناقص‌تر یا کم‌اعتمادتر می‌کند."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"A speaker says: \"It wasn’t the cost, and it wasn’t the timing. Really, it was the location.\" Which option do you choose?","options":["the location","the cost","the timing"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Two options are ruled out with \"it wasn’t\"; \"really\" gives the answer.","tr":"İki seçenek \"değildi\" ile eleniyor; \"really\" cevabı veriyor.","fa":"دو گزینه با «نبود» رد می‌شوند؛ «really» جواب را می‌دهد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"Their guide is free, but so are most of them. What made it different was the music.\" Which feature matches this guide?","options":["It is free.","It is short.","It uses music."],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Free is true but common; \"what made it different\" gives the answer.","tr":"Ücretsiz olması doğru ama yaygın; \"onu farklı kılan şey\" cevabı veriyor.","fa":"رایگان بودن درست است، اما رایج؛ «چیزی که آن را متفاوت کرد» جواب را می‌دهد."}}],"id":"c-x07-l3-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-07","unit":"x07-l3"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
